# CVE-2025-64756 - glob CLI command injection [HISTORICAL EXAMPLE - RESOLVED]
# Affects: glob package (transitive dependency of Gemini CLI)
# Issue: Command injection via -c/--cmd flag with shell:true
# Risk: LOW - Requires explicit use of glob CLI with -c flag, which is rare in dev workflows
# Status: RESOLVED - Gemini CLI 0.17.0 upgraded to glob@12.0.0 (patched)
# Fixed Versions: glob@10.5.0+ and glob@11.1.0+
# Timeline:
#   - 2025-11-18: CVE added to ignore list (Gemini CLI 0.15.4 used vulnerable glob@10.4.5)
#   - 2025-11-20: Gemini CLI 0.17.0 released with glob@12.0.0
#   - 2025-11-21: Container updated to Gemini CLI 0.17.0, CVE removed
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@google/gemini-cli
#   - Verify: npm view @google/gemini-cli@<version> dependencies.glob
# Review: Check for updates when new versions are released
# DO NOT UNCOMMENT - This is a resolved example for documentation purposes
# CVE-2025-64756

# ############################## End of example ##################################

# Last reviewed: 2026-01-14 (CVE triage: Added Hono JWT CVEs; Versions: Claude Code 2.1.1, Gemini CLI 0.23.0, Goose 1.19.0)

# CVE-2026-0621 - MCP SDK ReDoS vulnerability
# Affects: @modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.25.1 (transitive dependency via Gemini CLI)
# Issue: Regular Expression Denial of Service vulnerability in MCP TypeScript SDK
# Risk: MEDIUM - ReDoS requires attacker-controlled input to reach vulnerable regex patterns
#       in the MCP SDK. Gemini CLI uses MCP for tool integration, not user input processing.
# Source: Gemini CLI depends on @modelcontextprotocol/sdk@^1.23.0, which resolves to 1.25.1
# Fixed Versions: Not yet available (as of 2026-01-07)
# Timeline:
#   - 2025-12-16: MCP SDK 1.25.1 published with vulnerability
#   - 2026-01-07: CVE detected during Gemini CLI 0.23.0 update, added to ignore list
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk
#   - Monitor: https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases
#   - Check: npm view @modelcontextprotocol/sdk versions | grep -E "1\.2[5-9]\.[2-9]|1\.[3-9]"
#   - Verify fix: npm explain @modelcontextprotocol/sdk after Gemini CLI updates
# Review: Weekly until patched version available - see GitHub issue for tracking
CVE-2026-0621

# CVE-2026-22817, CVE-2026-22818 - Hono JWT algorithm confusion vulnerabilities
# Affects: hono@4.11.3 (transitive dependency via Claude Code 2.1.1 or Gemini CLI 0.23.0)
# Issue: JWT algorithm confusion in Hono's JWT and JWK/JWKS middleware allows
#        forged token acceptance when explicit algorithm configuration is missing
# Risk: LOW - Despite HIGH severity (CVSS 8.2), vulnerable code is not executed
#       Container provides CLI tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Goose), NOT web services
#       - No web server or HTTP endpoints exposed
#       - No JWT token processing or authentication
#       - Hono's JWT middleware is not invoked in CLI workflows
#       - Vulnerable code path is unreachable in this deployment context
# Fixed Versions: hono@4.11.4+
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-01-13: CVEs disclosed by Hono project
#   - 2026-01-14: Detected during nightly Trivy scan, added to ignore list
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@anthropic-ai/claude-code
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@google/gemini-cli
#   - Check: npm view @anthropic-ai/claude-code versions | tail -5
#   - Check: npm view @google/gemini-cli versions | tail -5
#   - Verify dependency: docker run --rm ghcr.io/rise8-us/xpai/ai-assistant-home:latest npm ls hono
# Review: Weekly until parent package updates to hono@4.11.4+
# CVSS: 8.2 HIGH (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:N)
# CWE: CWE-347 (Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature)
CVE-2026-22817
CVE-2026-22818